Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:48:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09638/11362] [outer-loop] Defuse the guard suite's own
 landmines: sandbox the watch set
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Team-lead review follow-up (pre-existing, from abc6a823ca): four tests
aimed REAL syscalls at the REAL record — write_text on README (x2,
direct and via symlink alias), os.replace onto README, and a probe
write into the deployed docs/blog/. Safe only while the guard works;
on regression — the single thing each test detects — the test's
failure mode WAS the incident (README overwritten with 'replacement'
before the assertion runs).

Converted to a sandbox_watch fixture that retargets the LIVE hook's
module watch set at a scratch tree and issues the SAME real syscalls
there: wiring coverage for the open and rename event paths is fully
preserved (proven: disabling either _audit_hook branch fails the
converted tests, with README byte-identical under the RED run — the
exact property the conversion buys). The unswapped configuration is
pinned read-only by test_default_watch_set_covers_the_real_record.

The worth-making evidence is permanent:
test_old_real_replace_shape_rewrites_the_record_when_the_guard_fails
breaks the guard deliberately and shows the OLD shape destroys the
sandbox README while the NEW synthetic shape touches nothing, with
the real README asserted untouched throughout. The rmtree and
tmp_path-copy false-positive tests were already sandbox-only and are
unchanged. 25 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
